&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW168921061 BCX8" style="-webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; clear: both; cursor: text; overflow: visible; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:calluna sans,calluna sans_embeddedfont,calluna sans_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;The M.J. Murdock Charitable Trust is a private, nonprofit foundation that has invested more than $1.5 billion in nonprofits serving the Pacific Northwest since 1975. For details, please visit our website&nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a class="Hyperlink SCXW168921061 BCX8" href="https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fmurdocktrust.org%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C01%7C%7C494d7ee50c3d4603db4408daf97b7fd7%7Cf48c5e8fd82b48b89bb00b981e40a413%7C0%7C1%7C638096606065612725%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=ZviKg%2FClSYsCzUtdFhmS34xBGUv7odCJAA%2BKPm6xXw0%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0" rel="noreferrer noopener" style="-webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; text-decoration-line: none;" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;span style="color:rgb(80, 201, 181); font-family:calluna sans,calluna sans_embeddedfont,calluna sans_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;murdocktrust.org&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:calluna sans,calluna sans_embeddedfont,calluna sans_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:calluna sans,calluna sans_embeddedfont,calluna sans_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width:100.0%"&gt;
     &lt;tbody&gt;
          &lt;tr&gt;
               &lt;td style="width:97.0%"&gt;
               &lt;p&gt;Sultan Sschool District: We will be on a 2-hour delay schedule for tomorrow, Thursday, December 11th, 2025. There will be no AM out of District transportation.&amp;nbsp; We will provide an update at 7:30 AM tomorrow.&lt;/p&gt;
               &lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;/tr&gt;
     &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PORTLAND, Ore. &lt;/strong&gt;&mdash; The Bureau of Land Management continues a highly successful prescribed burn season, having treated more than &lt;strong&gt;18,000&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;acres&lt;/strong&gt; of public lands since the beginning of September. These efforts reduce hazardous fuels, improve wildlife habitat, and build more resilient landscapes across the region.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&ldquo;BLM fire staff have stayed prepared, so we&rsquo;re ready to capitalize on windows with the safest burning conditions,&rdquo; said Michael Solheim, fire management specialist. &ldquo;We&rsquo;ve been waiting for rain and for drought conditions to gradually improve. These conditions are essential to executing treatments effectively and maintaining our commitment to protect communities and restore landscape resilience.&rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Prescribed burning is one of the most effective tools land managers have to reduce excessive vegetation and restore native ecosystems. This season&rsquo;s burns have helped return nutrients to the soil, stimulate new plant growth, and maintain open spaces, while also supporting a sustained yield of timber and forage for cattle.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Many landscapes in Oregon and Washington have evolved with fire, making it a vital, natural process. Through careful application, prescribed burning helps maintain watershed health, protect water quality, and sustain the biodiversity that characterizes these fire-adapted ecosystems.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Crews rely on detailed weather monitoring, fire-modeling tools and careful planning to ensure burns are conducted safely and effectively. The BLM works closely with rural fire departments, federal and state agencies, and nonprofit partners throughout the year to focus on critical work.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&ldquo;We&rsquo;re grateful to our neighbors for supporting this work,&rdquo; said Solheim. &ldquo;Prescribed fire requires patience, especially when smoke is visible, but it&rsquo;s an investment in long-term safety and healthier public lands.&rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For more information about prescribed fire and ongoing fuel reduction efforts, visit the BLM&rsquo;s &lt;a href="https://www.blm.gov/programs/public-safety-and-fire/fire/state-info/oregon-washington/prescribed-fire"&gt;website&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;-BLM-&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The BLM manages about 245 million acres of public land located primarily in 12 western states, including Alaska, on behalf of the American people. The BLM also administers 700 million acres of sub-surface mineral estate throughout the nation. Our mission is to sustain the health, diversity, and productivity of America&rsquo;s public lands for the use and enjoyment of present and future generations.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW24002932 BCX0" style="margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; -webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; overflow: visible; cursor: text; clear: both; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;VALE, Ore.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&mdash; The Bureau of Land Management recently approved the expansion of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;lithium exploration activities in southern Malheur County, about 20 miles west of McDermitt, Nev.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW24002932 BCX0" style="margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; -webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; overflow: visible; cursor: text; clear: both; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;With this approval, HiTech Minerals, Inc. is authorized to conduct lithium mineral exploration activities over the course of five years. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;Lithium has been on the Department of the Interior&rsquo;s &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a class="Hyperlink SCXW24002932 BCX0" href="https://www.doi.gov/pressreleases/interior-department-releases-final-2025-list-critical-minerals" rel="noreferrer noopener" style="margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; -webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; text-decoration-line: none;" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 255); font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;list of critical minerals&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt; since the list was established in 2017.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW24002932 BCX0" style="margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; -webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; overflow: visible; cursor: text; clear: both; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW24002932 BCX0" style="margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; -webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; overflow: visible; cursor: text; clear: both; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&ldquo;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;The HiTech lithium exploration project represents a significant step toward achieving the nation&rsquo;s energy goals and reducing dependence on foreign critical minerals&mdash;key priorities under the President&rsquo;s agenda&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;,&rdquo; said &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BLM Acting Malheur Field Manager Tara McLain&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW24002932 BCX0" style="margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; -webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; overflow: visible; cursor: text; clear: both; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW24002932 BCX0" style="margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; -webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; overflow: visible; cursor: text; clear: both; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;The project includes disturbance of up to 73 total acres created by 168 exploration drill sites across 7,200 acres of public lands, the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;construction of 22 miles of new access routes, and other temporary disturbances to store necessary equipment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW24002932 BCX0" style="margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; -webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; overflow: visible; cursor: text; clear: both; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW24002932 BCX0" style="margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; -webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; overflow: visible; cursor: text; clear: both; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;E&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;xploration drilling would occur annually between July 1 and November 30 for up to five years, and concurrent reclamation of the disturbances would occur after each drill season. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;Subsurface hydrological, geophysical, and geochemical data may be collected during the proposed drilling activities as well.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:roboto,roboto_embeddedfont,roboto_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

